  "query_preview": "../Tuesday through Thursday/...Unsettled weather will \ncontinue into at least the beginning of this period as low \npressure meanders while slowly weakening over south-central \nAlaska. The heaviest rainfall Tuesday into early Wednesday will \nlikely be centered over the northeast Gulf Coast and northern \npanhandle with lighter amounts farther south. A few thunderstorms \nstill also appear possible, especially over the coastal waters, \nbut we did not include thunder in the forecast at this time given \nthe uncertainty and anticipated low coverage. As the \naforementioned low finally disintegrates on Thursday, we should \nsee an overall improvement in conditions. A separate, more intense\nlow pressure system may approach the southern panhandle late \nThursday and beyond, but model agreement on the track and timing \nof the system is quite low. This will be monitored closely in \nfuture forecasts. After this potential system, high pressure will \nattempt to at least briefly build into the Gulf.",
